# Deliberately minimal. core.autocrlf=true rewrites EOLs on checkout, which is
# fine everywhere except files whose exact checkout bytes are a governed
# invariant. Only one path qualifies (audited 2026-08-08).
#
# Excluded by audit, not oversight:
#   - the 118 tracked PNGs are already binary (-text) to Git, so every frozen
#     reference.png SHA contract is inherently safe;
#   - supabase/migrations/*.sql are hashed against HEAD, but those suites
#     already normalize CRLF on both sides (c3-static.mjs:29,
#     ct-static.mjs:33, asm-static.mjs norm()), and 6 of 12 sit CRLF today
#     and pass — pinning them would rewrite files for no gain;
#   - _checkpoint-evidence/*.json are historical records with no consumer.
#
# No renormalization was run. The path below is already LF, so this pins the
# status quo rather than changing it.

# Exact-byte checkout invariant. This file carries the pinned SHA-256 of the 12
# frozen reference.png files, screenCount 36, every Figma node record, and (as of
# 2026-08-08) the machine-readable currentReferencePack mapping that resolves the
# three irregular /reference/ directory names. Without -text a Windows clone
# checks it out CRLF, changing its size and SHA, so the invariant would be
# machine-local instead of reproducible. Q-28 exists because a PowerShell
# ConvertTo-Json round-trip already corrupted this exact file once in Phase A2.
#
# Canonical bytes (verify after any authorized edit):
#   size    55434
#   sha256  598c714a37ededf200881deb18e1f92d882c77f784be8c91782ec04288a0b10f
#
# KNOWN LIMIT on the "reproducible on a fresh Windows clone" premise, found by
# adversarial review and PRE-EXISTING (not introduced by this rule):
# core.longpaths is unset, and the longest tracked path is 113 chars
#   UI_REFERENCE_FINAL_MVP/reference/Auth 04 - All Users - Forgot Password/
#   Auth 04 - All Users - Forgot Password.html
# so cloning into a root deeper than ~145 chars fails checkout with
# "Filename too long" (exit 128). Clone shallow, or set core.longpaths=true.
# Not fixed here: it is a machine/clone-side setting, not a repository byte
# invariant, and changing it is outside a UI-authority synchronization.
UI_REFERENCE_FINAL_MVP/UI_PACK_MANIFEST.json -text
